Running 2e on old texts, I find that a primary documentstyle that includes
a standard one (mine is a `UK version' of article) fails to include
substyles (i.e., \documentstyle[others,...]{ukart} doesn't load
others.sty, ...).  I've formally reported this through the proper channel.

I've produced two packages by hacking at old things I regularly use:

  changebar.sty  a version of that which is in CTAN; uses package option
                 instead of the \driver command
  footnote.sty   Dominik/Chris's fnpara, Brian Schellenberger's "footnotes
                 numbered per page", and footnote mark := symbol, each
                 separately selectable by options

Pro tem, I've mounted them for anon ftp in ftp.cl.cam.ac.uk:/pegasus/tex/

They're rather rough at the moment, just the wherewithal to explore the
business of writing stuff for LaTeX2e; if no-one else is working on
similar things, I'll tidy them up and submit them to an archive (in
particular, the changebar was developed from a docstripped original I
happened to have at home...)

